    // tiny — any per-channel Poisson/sky/read noise then got over-amplified
    // by the stretch, producing the chromatic patchiness that drowned the
    // model's smooth filaments. With direct RGB, all three channels carry
    // signal at comparable magnitudes and the per-channel noise stretches
    // proportionally — chrominance noise is preserved (per user request to
    // keep RGB chrominance noise consistent), but it's no longer artificially
    // amplified relative to the signal. Channel mode "broadband_rgb" in
    // deriveSystem makes all three apply flt.broadband_pass uniformly, so
    // narrowband filters dim the whole galaxy by the same factor as a real
    // OSC sensor would (instead of selectively preserving ha/oiii channels
    // through their line passes — which was wrong for a broadband target). v946: the H-alpha HII-knot component is the exception — encode() boosts it by ha_pass/broadband_pass so it survives narrowband as line emission, while the continuum still rides broadband_pass.
