      // true angular size on the sensor (v900 unification), so deep-zoom
      // views \u2014 matchZoom + small zoomDetailFraction on a long-focal-length
      // system \u2014 sample the bake at angular density way finer than the v812
      // 3\u2033/basepx single-bake convention. To deliver smooth crater rims
      // there, we bake the same procedural model (same Mulberry32 seed,
      // same maria, same crater list) at three angular-extent levels via a
      // zoom_factor scalar in the generator: 1\u00d7 (coarse), 2.4\u00d7 (mid), 6\u00d7
      // (fine). Each level is the same 1280\u00d7800 grid, so memory cost per
      // level is 4\u202fMB. Total worst case across all three: 12\u202fMB.
      //
      // Level selection: pick the smallest bake whose angular extent \u2265 the
      // displayed field. So a 243\u2033 matchZoom view of sysB lands on L2 (400\u2033
      // bake at 0.5\u2033/basepx) \u2014 crater rims sampled at ~3\u00d7 the cam pixel
      // scale, visually curved. A wide native FOV lands on L0 (2400\u2033 bake at
      // 3\u2033/basepx) where the moon is a small disc anyway and the coarse
      // sampling is invisible.
      //
      // 0.5\u2033/basepx is the floor (L2). Finer than that didn't seem worth
      // the GPU memory \u2014 it's below typical seeing-limit resolution and
      // exceeds the 500\u202fmm-aperture diffraction limit (~0.28\u2033). The crater
      // count was also halved to 2000 (see runMoonBakeGpu / gen_moonDiscMap)
